# API SPECIFICATION
**System:** GridVision SCADA Management API
**Version:** 2.0.3
**Domain:** Energy / Critical Infrastructure / Grid Management
**Classification:** CUI // CRITICAL INFRASTRUCTURE

## 1. Overview
GridVision exposes a GraphQL API to authorized grid operators. Each utility company is a separate `operator_id`. The JWT encodes `user_id`, `role` (one of `field_tech`, `grid_operator`, `regional_admin`), and `operator_id`.

## 2. GraphQL Schema
```graphql
type Substation {
  substationId: ID!
  operatorId: ID!
  name: String!
  gridZone: String
  maintenanceSchedule: [MaintenanceEvent!]
  controlParameters: ControlConfig    # RESTRICTED: operator staff only
  alarmHistory: [AlarmEvent!]         # RESTRICTED: regional_admin only
}

type ControlConfig {
  voltageSetpoint: Float
  loadBalancingMode: String
  emergencyShutdownEnabled: Boolean
  remoteControlEnabled: Boolean
}

type Query {
  getSubstation(id: ID!): Substation
  listSubstations(operatorId: ID): [Substation!]
}
```

## 3. Resolver Implementation
```javascript
// Substation resolver
const substationResolver = {
  Query: {
    getSubstation: async (_, { id }, ctx) => {
      // Operator isolation
      const sub = await db.substations.findById(id);
      if (sub.operatorId !== ctx.jwt.operatorId) throw new ForbiddenError();
      return sub;  // Returns full Substation object
    }
  },
  Substation: {
    // No field-level resolver guards — all child resolvers inherit parent
    controlParameters: (parent) => db.controlConfigs.findBySubstation(parent.substationId),
    alarmHistory: (parent) => db.alarms.findBySubstation(parent.substationId),
  }
};
```

**Note:** The `Substation` resolver enforces `operatorId` matching. However, the nested field resolvers (`controlParameters`, `alarmHistory`) do not re-check the caller's `role`. A `field_tech` can access `controlParameters` and `alarmHistory` fields by including them in the selection set — the role restriction is documented but not implemented in the resolver.

